    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, led by the undeniable elite-tier production of **Kyle Tucker** (82.82) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Both hitters benefit from an advantageous matchup against Zack Littell and Jack Kochanowicz respectively; their strong base projections are bolstered significantly by high-upside SP skill ratings (+19% and +18%) and favorable batting order slots. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) also projects as a high-floor start, capitalizing on a potent platoon edge against Shane Baz, while **Jackson Merrill** (68.69) and **Andy Pages** (67.46) round out a formidable top-of-the-order attack that prioritizes both run production and efficiency in stolen base environments.\n\nThe decision to keep **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (49.68) on the bench was the most difficult pivot of the day. Despite his high base projection, his score was suppressed by a daunting matchup against Ty Madden (xERA 2.12), causing him to fall just short of the threshold required to displace the more efficient matchups held by **Heliot Ramos** and **Josh Jung**. Meanwhile, **Brady House** (59.63) managed to secure a spot due to the high-leverage nature of Shane Baz\u2019s slow delivery, which adds a crucial +2% boost to our team\u2019s emphasis on stolen base aggression. \n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as every selection is currently contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" status. We are particularly monitoring **Drake Baldwin** (47.58); while his offensive profile is currently elevated by a #1 order projection, his score is actively dragged down by the elite 2.92 xERA of opposing pitcher Connelly Early. Managers should note that while **Sam Antonacci** (54.85) is slotted in for his elite 0.403 xwOBA, his score is sensitive to the 3.76 xERA of Edward Cabrera; any negative shift in the official batting order for **Sam Antonacci** or **Drake Baldwin** may necessitate an immediate reassessment of their utility for the daily game cap.",
